A||N||3||chris6878||changing to the newer style headlight motors?||||3||
Z||000000||chris6878||05-25-2000||12:20 PM||||My daily driver is a 85 SE V6 and it has the headlight syndrome. I have an 87 coupe parts car with the newer stlye headlight motors. One of the motors was toasted when it was wrecked.  But the other motor and wiring harness are still there. Besides getting the other motor, will every thing else just plug and play on the wiring harness.||||reg||3
Z||000001||BN Boomer||05-25-2000||01:34 PM||||I recently did this same swap from my 87 Coupe parts car to my 85 GT. Yes, almost everything about this swap is simple nuts, bolts, and electrical plugs. I say "almost" because on the 87 there is a control module between the driver's side fender and firewall forward of the front wheel that is sort of a pain to get out. You'll need to at least remove the rivet and screws and pull back the fender and front fascia to get at the screws holding this module in place. When putting it into your 85, you'll have to decide whether to go to the pain of putting it back in there or relocating it somewhere inside the headlight compartment. Either way, you'll need to drill a couple of holes to install it. Also plan on removing the hoods, the A/C condensor mounting bolts, and at least loosening the radiator mounting bolts on both cars in order to fish the wiring wiring harness out from in front of the radiator of the 87 and then reinstalling it in the 85. It takes a bit of time to do, but isn't difficult and is better and looks cleaner than splicing wiring harnesses, in my opion.<P>Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000002||80's BOY||05-25-2000||02:23 PM||||boy does this sound familiar......is this what i have to look forward to?? can't you just cut the wires from the 85 and reconnect to the 87 harnesses. i'm sure the colors are the same, are'nt they??||||reg||11
Z||000003||theogre||05-25-2000||02:28 PM||||I wondered where they hid that bloody thing.<P>If it will reach there, I think I'd just attach it to the tire side of the front wall of the storage compartment. Then it won't get crap all over it, and it will be easy to get to if it ever croaks. There's plenty of room there for it.||||reg||1
